{"question_id": "V2-dev-RPT-en-T2-002", "approach": "B1", "approach_base": "B1", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "D", "corpus_set": "D_en", "answer_text": "Delivery Hero treats the pre-August 2021 model risk as probable and has recognized provisions, while the post-August 2021 model risk is treated as possible but not probable and disclosed only as a contingency. Glovo decided to progressively move to an employment-based model in Spain from 2025.\n\n- For the model operated by Glovo until August 2021, the risk is more likely than not to materialize, so appropriate provisions are reflected in the Consolidated Financial Statements (Strategic Risks, [1]).\n- For the model in place since August 2021 (Glovo Spain), the risk is deemed possible but not probable, so it is disclosed as a contingency of approximately €440.0 million to €770.0 million, with no provision recognized (Strategic Risks [1]; Contingencies [2]; Auditor's Report [5]).\n- In December 2024, Glovo's management decided to progressively move to an employment-based model in Spain, effective 2025, to avoid further legal uncertainties (Strategic Risks [3]; Business development by segment [4]).\n- Glovo will defend the self-employed status through all available instances and continue cooperating with the Spanish authorities, while bank guarantees were provided in 2024 to secure liabilities claimed for the pre-August 2021 model (Strategic Risks, [3]).", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 727 chars]", "doc_id": "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en", "section_id": "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::h201", "unit_ids": ["D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::p128_b9"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 0, "span": [466060, 466787], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 788 chars]", "doc_id": "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en", "section_id": "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::h320", "unit_ids": ["D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::p2